    {
      "file": "tmp/sources/ext-apps/examples/pdf-server/server.ts",
      "line": 1451,
      "kind": "registerAppTool",
      "name": "display_pdf",
      "description": {
        "text": "disableInteract\n        ? `Show and render a PDF in a read-only viewer.\n\nUse this tool when the user wants to view or read a PDF. The renderer displays the document for viewing. The widget exposes app-registered tools for page navigation, text extraction, searching, and zoom control.\n\nAccepts local files (use list_pdfs), client MCP root directories, or any HTTPS URL.`\n        : `Open a PDF in an interactive viewer. Call this ONCE per PDF.\n\n**All follow-up actions go through the \\`interact\\` tool** with the returned viewUUID â€” annotating, signing, stamping, filling forms, navigating, searching, extracting text/screenshots. Calling display_pdf again creates a SEPARATE viewer with a different viewUUID â€” interact calls using the new UUID will not reach the viewer the user already sees.\n\nReturns a viewUUID in structuredContent. Pass it to \\`interact\\`:\n- add_annotations, update_annotations, remove_annotations, highlight_text\n- fill_form (fill PDF form fields)\n- navigate, search, find, search_navigate, zoom\n- get_text, get_screenshot, get_viewer_state (extract content / read selection & current page)\n- save_as (write annotated PDF to disk)\n\nAccepts local files (use list_pdfs), client MCP root directories, or any HTTPS URL.\nSet \\`elicit_form_inputs\\` to true to prompt the user to fill form fields before display.`",
        "exact": false
      },
      "title": {
        "text": "Display PDF",
        "exact": true
      },
      "input": "z.object({\n        url: z\n          .string()\n          .default(DEFAULT_PDF)\n          .describe(\"PDF URL or local file path\"),\n        page: z.number().min(1).default(1).describe(\"Initial page\"),\n        ...(disableInteract\n          ? {}\n          : {\n              elicit_form_inputs: z\n                .boolean()\n                .default(false)\n                .describe(\n                  \"If true and the PDF has form fields, prompt the user to fill them before displaying\",\n                ),\n            }),\n      })",
      "inputWording": [
        {
          "source": "url: z\n          .string()\n          .default(DEFAULT_PDF)\n          .describe(\"PDF URL or local file path\")",
          "wording": {
            "text": "PDF URL or local file path",
            "exact": true
          }
        },
        {
          "source": "page: z.number().min(1).default(1).describe(\"Initial page\")",
          "wording": {
            "text": "Initial page",
            "exact": true
          }
        },
        {
          "source": "elicit_form_inputs: z\n                .boolean()\n                .default(false)\n                .describe(\n                  \"If true and the PDF has form fields, prompt the user to fill them before displaying\",\n                )",
          "wording": {
            "text": "If true and the PDF has form fields, prompt the user to fill them before displaying",
            "exact": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "metadata": "{ ui: { resourceUri: RESOURCE_URI } }",
      "config": "{\n      title: \"Display PDF\",\n      description: disableInteract\n        ? `Show and render a PDF in a read-only viewer.\n\nUse this tool when the user wants to view or read a PDF. The renderer displays the document for viewing. The widget exposes app-registered tools for page navigation, text extraction, searching, and zoom control.\n\nAccepts local files (use list_pdfs), client MCP root directories, or any HTTPS URL.`\n        : `Open a PDF in an interactive viewer. Call this ONCE per PDF.\n\n**All follow-up actions go through the \\`interact\\` tool** with the returned viewUUID â€” annotating, signing, stamping, filling forms, navigating, searching, extracting text/screenshots. Calling display_pdf again creates a SEPARATE viewer with a different viewUUID â€” interact calls using the new UUID will not reach the viewer the user already sees.\n\nReturns a viewUUID in structuredContent. Pass it to \\`interact\\`:\n- add_annotations, update_annotations, remove_annotations, highlight_text\n- fill_form (fill PDF form fields)\n- navigate, search, find, search_navigate, zoom\n- get_text, get_screenshot, get_viewer_state (extract content / read selection & current page)\n- save_as (write annotated PDF to disk)\n\nAccepts local files (use list_pdfs), client MCP root directories, or any HTTPS URL.\nSet \\`elicit_form_inputs\\` to true to prompt the user to fill form fields before display.`,\n      inputSchema: z.object({\n        url: z\n          .string()\n          .default(DEFAULT_PDF)\n          .describe(\"PDF URL or local file path\"),\n        page: z.number().min(1).default(1).describe(\"Initial page\"),\n        ...(disableInteract\n          ? {}\n          : {\n              elicit_form_inputs: z\n                .boolean()\n                .default(false)\n                .describe(\n                  \"If true and the PDF has form fields, prompt the user to fill them before displaying\",\n                ),\n            }),\n      }),\n      outputSchema: z.object({\n        viewUUID: z\n          .string()\n          .describe(\n            \"UUID for this viewer instance\" +\n              (disableInteract ? \"\" : \" â€” pass to interact tool\"),\n          ),\n        url: z.string(),\n        initialPage: z.number(),\n        totalBytes: z.number(),\n        formFieldValues: z\n          .record(z.string(), z.union([z.string(), z.boolean()]))\n          .optional()\n          .describe(\"Form field values filled by the user via elicitation\"),\n        formFields: z\n          .array(\n            z.object({\n              name: z.string(),\n              type: z.string(),\n              page: z.number(),\n              label: z.string().optional(),\n              x: z.number(),\n              y: z.number(),\n              width: z.number(),\n              height: z.number(),\n              exportValue: z\n                .string()\n                .optional()\n                .describe(\"Radio button value â€” pass this to fill_form\"),\n              options: z\n                .array(z.string())\n                .optional()\n                .describe(\"Dropdown/listbox option values\"),\n            }),\n          )\n          .optional()\n          .describe(\n            \"Form fields with bounding boxes in model coordinates (top-left origin)\",\n          ),\n      }),\n      _meta: { ui: { resourceUri: RESOURCE_URI } },\n    }",
      "resultTexts": [
        {
          "text": "validation.error!",
          "exact": false
